  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CIRCUITOS DE AGROECOLGICOS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smallholder farmers in Brazil struggle to market their products at a reasonable price, and as a result their livelihoods and ability to support their families suffer. At the IAF, we support community-led solutions to expand economic opportunity in Brazil. Taba Fortalecimento Comunitrio (Taba) works with two major sustainable agriculture networks in Brazil to increase the income of members, including indigenous people and Afro-Brazilians, through training, technical assistance, and micro loans. Taba is supporting these networks to increase their agricultural productivity, upgrade agro-processing facilities, expand organic certifications, develop value-added products, improve marketing circuits, and install a sales outlet in the city of So Paulo. Taba&apos;s activities promote smallholder agriculture and ensure meaningful opportunities for communities to thrive.</narrative>
  </description>
